    "Le facteur B.~C impose B = 1 et C = 0. Il reste (A + 1).(~A + 0 + ~D) = ~A + ~D : faux seulement pour A = D = 1. Avec B = 1, C = 0, les lignes à 1 sont A, D = 00, 01, 10.": "The factor B.~C forces B = 1 and C = 0. What remains is (A + 1).(~A + 0 + ~D) = ~A + ~D: false only for A = D = 1. With B = 1, C = 0, the rows equal to 1 are A, D = 00, 01, 10.",
    "C’est un produit de sommes : on complète chaque somme. (A + ~B) → (A + ~B + C).(A + ~B + ~C) ; (~B + C) → (A + ~B + C).(~A + ~B + C). Le maxterme (A + ~B + C) n’est écrit qu’une fois.": "This is a product of sums: complete each sum. (A + ~B) → (A + ~B + C).(A + ~B + ~C); (~B + C) → (A + ~B + C).(~A + ~B + C). The maxterm (A + ~B + C) is written only once.",
